hpy-013.text:
The solution uses dynamic programming with two rows to keep track of whether the prefix of the pattern matches the prefix of the string. For each character of the pattern we update the current row based on the previous row, handling `*` as a wildcard that can match zero or more characters and `?` as a single‑character wildcard. This yields an O(|pattern|·|s|) time and O(|s|) space algorithm, avoiding exponential backtracking.

ANSWER:
```python
def wildcard_match(pattern, s):
    m, n = len(pattern), len(s)
    prev = [False] * (n + 1)
    prev[0] = True
    for j in range(1, n + 1):
        prev[j] = False

    for i in range(1, m + 1):
        cur = [False] * (n + 1)
        if pattern[i - 1] == '*':
            cur[0] = prev[0]
            for j in range(1, n + 1):
                cur[j] = cur[j - 1] or prev[j]
        else:
            for j in range(1, n + 1):
                if pattern[i - 1] == '?' or pattern[i - 1] == s[j - 1]:
                    cur[j] = prev[j - 1]
                else:
                    cur[j] = False
        prev = cur

    return prev[n]
```

