The `singleFlight` function maintains a map of pending promises keyed by the loader argument, ensuring that concurrent calls with the same key share the same promise. When the promise resolves or rejects, the entry is removed so subsequent calls trigger a new execution, and rejections are propagated to all waiters without caching.

