I will implement `chunkAsync` as an async generator that buffers items from the source iterable, pulling at most `size` items ahead of what the consumer has requested to keep the operation lazy. The generator will handle both synchronous and asynchronous iterables by normalizing them to async iteration, and it will call the source’s `return()` method when the consumer stops early to clean up resources.

ANSWER:
```javascript
module.exports = async function* chunkAsync(source, size) {
  if (size <= 0) throw new Error('size must be positive');
  const iterator = source[Symbol.asyncIterator]
    ? source[Symbol.asyncIterator]()
    : {
        next: () => Promise.resolve({ value: source.next(), done: false }),
        return: (value) => {
          if (source.return) return source.return(value);
          return Promise.resolve({ value, done: true });
        },
      };
  const buffer = [];
  try {
    while (true) {
      if (buffer.length === 0) {
        const { value, done } = await iterator.next();
        if (done) break;
        buffer.push(value);
      }
      const chunk = [];
      while (chunk.length < size && buffer.length > 0) {
        chunk.push(buffer.shift());
      }
      if (chunk.length === 0) break;
      yield chunk;
    }
  } finally {
    if (iterator.return) await iterator.return();
  }
};
