I will implement `pick` and `omit` using mapped types and conditional types to preserve the optionality and readonly modifiers of the surviving properties. The functions will accept only keys that exist on the object, ensuring type safety at compile time. For `pick`, I'll use a mapped type to select only the specified keys, and for `omit`, I'll exclude the specified keys while preserving the rest. Edge cases include handling empty key arrays and ensuring the resulting types are correctly inferred.

